**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.PlannerReportTests`

**How to implement.** A look at a plate, and what one look sees of each tensor component, by the layer-1 rules (001 §M 'what each cut sees: a c-cut at normal incidence sees n_o only (and g33); n_e needs oblique incidence or an a-cut', 'activity along birefringent directions needs full-Mueller or HAUP-class measurements', 'intensity-only detectors lose phase'; the S14.1 brief). The rules speak the parameterization the study engine fits, the engine's bi-anisotropic rho, along whose propagation direction the TRANSVERSE gyration acts and g33 does not (`MuellerInverse.fs:62` module header), because the Planner reports on the study engine's unknowns and `MuellerInverseTests` asserts `C1 is completely blind to g33`; 001's '(and g33)' is the crystallographic reading. So the crystallographic projection `gyrationProjection`, which that header and its own doc (`MuellerInverse.fs:gyrationProjection`) say is deliberately not used to predict this engine, is not called; the Snell cap reuses `internalAngle` (step 468) and the cut geometry `orientForCut` (step 466). Every rule is first order: what a look's normalized reading depends on linearly. (1) New `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MeasurementPlanner.fs`, `module MeasurementPlanner` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, appended at the end of the Domain compile list after `PlannerSymmetry.fs` (one `<Compile>` line, no comment). Module doc: the Measurement Planner's inputs from a kit and its structural recoverability report (spec 0050 S14.1). Each doc below is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.1; every case name has two words; no `bool` appears. (2) `DetectorReach` = `FullMuellerReach` (a full Mueller matrix: a polarimeter, or the HAUP class, an intensity detector between a polarizer and an analyzer) | `EllipsometricReach` (Psi and Delta, the ratio of the diagonal Jones elements) | `IntensityOnlyReach` (S0 alone, its level scaled by the detector's gain, 001 §I). (3) `LookTilt` = `NormalIncidenceLook | ObliqueIncidenceLook` and `AxisAspect` = `TransverseAxis | LongitudinalAxis`. (4) `PlannerLook = { normalAxisOpt : CrystalAxis option; incidence : IncidenceAngle; observable : Observable; reach : DetectorReach }`, one measurement a kit or a design makes of a plate: the principal axis on its normal (step 466), the external incidence, T or R (`MuellerInverse.fs:Observable`) and what its detector records. `member this.tilt : LookTilt` is `NormalIncidenceLook` when `this.incidence.value` equals `IncidenceAngle.normal.value` (`Fields.fs:29`) and `ObliqueIncidenceLook` otherwise. `member this.aspectOf (axis : CrystalAxis) : AxisAspect` is `LongitudinalAxis` when the look is at normal incidence and `normalAxisOpt` is `Some axis`, and `TransverseAxis` otherwise: off normal incidence the refracted wave runs at a non-zero internal angle to the normal, so no principal axis lies along it. (5) `type MeasurementConfiguration with member this.plannerLookWith (reach : DetectorReach) : PlannerLook` (`MuellerInverse.fs:MeasurementConfiguration`): `{ normalAxisOpt = this.cut.normalAxisOpt; incidence = this.incidenceAngle; observable = this.observable; reach = reach }`, so a spec 0044 design is read as looks with nothing transcribed. (6) `LookSight` = `SeenInLook | AlongPropagationInLook | NormalIncidenceInLook | NoRetardanceInLook | ReachMissesInLook`. (7) On `PlannerLook`, `member this.sightOf (crystal : CrystalParameters) (component : TensorComponent) : LookSight`, where an axis is transverse when `aspectOf` answers `TransverseAxis`: (a) `PrincipalIndexComponent axes`: `AlongPropagationInLook` when no axis of `axes` is transverse; otherwise `SeenInLook` for an oblique look (the Fresnel amplitudes and the internal angle move with the index, specs/0044/.manual/004 §3.2); otherwise, at normal incidence, `SeenInLook` when the reach is not `IntensityOnlyReach` and the transverse axes are occupied by two or more distinct `PrincipalIndexComponent`s of `crystal.components` (linear retardance, whose phase carries the indices), and `NoRetardanceInLook` otherwise: a uniaxial plate along its optic axis is a pure rotator whose normalized matrix carries no index at first order (`MuellerInverseTests`' `C1 alone cannot determine three of the four constants`), and an intensity-only reading records no retardance while the gain takes its level. (b) `GyrationDiagonalComponent axes`: `AlongPropagationInLook` when no axis is transverse; `SeenInLook` under `FullMuellerReach`; `ReachMissesInLook` otherwise (optical activity rotates the polarization, which Psi and Delta and an intensity without an analyzer do not record at first order, and along a birefringent direction it is buried under the retardance, 001 §M). (c) `GyrationOffDiagonalComponent _`: `NormalIncidenceInLook` for a normal-incidence look at a plate with a principal axis on its normal (the engine's rho couples the off-diagonal components through the wave's longitudinal field, which exists only off normal incidence: `BiaxialInverseTests.fs:42-48` and `the cuts buy the gyration DIAGONAL and only the tilt buys its OFF-DIAGONAL`); otherwise `SeenInLook` under `FullMuellerReach` and `ReachMissesInLook` under another reach. (d) `AbsorptionDiagonalComponent axis`: `SeenInLook` when the axis is transverse, else `AlongPropagationInLook`. (e) `AbsorptionOffDiagonalComponent pair`: `SeenInLook` when both axes are transverse, else `AlongPropagationInLook` (a component coupling the propagation axis reaches the transverse response only at second order). A plate with no principal axis on its normal has every axis transverse, so the Planner never calls a component unseen through it; layer 2 (S14.2) measures such a plate. No other type or member is added. Tests: new `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlannerReportTests.fs`, `module PlannerReportTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over test-local records written as literals (step 465's uniaxial, triclinic and absorbing probes) and looks written as records, an oblique look being at `IncidenceAngle.create (Angle.degree 30.0<Berreman.Constants.deg>)`. `a look sees a component only through an axis transverse to its propagation`: at a z-cut at normal incidence, transmitted, `FullMuellerReach`, the uniaxial n_e and g33 are `AlongPropagationInLook` and g11 `SeenInLook`; at the same plate oblique, n_e and g33 are `SeenInLook`; at an x-cut at normal incidence g33 is `SeenInLook`; `aspectOf` answers `LongitudinalAxis` for the 3-axis and `TransverseAxis` for the 1-axis at the normal z-cut, `TransverseAxis` for every axis oblique and at normal incidence on a plate whose `normalAxisOpt` is `None`. `an index needs linear retardance at normal incidence, or an oblique look`: the uniaxial n_o is `NoRetardanceInLook` at the normal z-cut, transmitted and reflected, and `SeenInLook` with n_e at the normal x-cut; the triclinic n1 and n2 are `SeenInLook` and n3 `AlongPropagationInLook` at the normal z-cut; under `IntensityOnlyReach` the uniaxial n_o is `NoRetardanceInLook` at the normal x-cut and `SeenInLook` at the oblique z-cut. `gyration needs a full Mueller reach, and an off-diagonal component an oblique look`: at the normal z-cut under `FullMuellerReach` the triclinic g12 is `NormalIncidenceInLook` and g11 `SeenInLook`; oblique, g12 and g13 are `SeenInLook`; under `EllipsometricReach` the uniaxial g33 at the normal x-cut and g11 at the normal z-cut are `ReachMissesInLook`; under `IntensityOnlyReach` the oblique triclinic g12 is `ReachMissesInLook`; and at normal incidence on a plate whose `normalAxisOpt` is `None` g12 is `SeenInLook` under `FullMuellerReach`. `an absorption component is seen through its transverse axes`: at the normal z-cut the absorbing e11 and e12 are `SeenInLook` and e33 and e13 `AlongPropagationInLook`; oblique, e33 and e13 are `SeenInLook`. `a measurement configuration is a look at its cut's normal axis, incidence and observable`: the configuration `{ cut = XCut; thickness = Thickness.mkm 20.0<Berreman.Constants.mkm>; incidenceAngle = IncidenceAngle.create (Angle.degree 30.0<Berreman.Constants.deg>); azimuth = SampleAzimuth.degree 45.0<Berreman.Constants.deg>; observable = ReflectedMueller; waveLength = WaveLength.nm 632.8<Berreman.Constants.nm> }}`'s `plannerLookWith EllipsometricReach` is the look of `FirstCrystalAxis`, that incidence, `ReflectedMueller` and `EllipsometricReach`, its tilt `ObliqueIncidenceLook`; the same configuration with `ZCut` at 0 degrees is a `NormalIncidenceLook` of `ThirdCrystalAxis`.

**Acceptance.** After the looks land, `PlannerLook.sightOf` MUST judge each component by the transverse, retardance, full-Mueller and off-normal rules, and `MeasurementConfiguration.plannerLookWith` MUST read a design's configuration as a look; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a look sees a component only through an axis transverse to its propagation`, `an index needs linear retardance at normal incidence, or an oblique look`, `gyration needs a full Mueller reach, and an off-diagonal component an oblique look`, `an absorption component is seen through its transverse axes` and `a measurement configuration is a look at its cut's normal axis, incidence and observable`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.
